        "rationale": "The tests cover each behavioral obligation in `requirements.sdk.graph.agent-harness.with_agent`.\n\n1. **Criteria obtain the cache's agent through `ValidationContext`.**\n   - `supplied_openai_backend_runs_independent_calls_against_a_local_transport` builds the domain with `ValidationCache::with_agent(config)`. It runs `Validator::verify` on a criterion that asks, and checks the requests that reach the local transport. They carry the configured model, the tools, the prompt and the tool results.\n   - `supplied_ollama_backend_delivers_tools_and_results_over_native_chat` does the same over the native Ollama chat endpoint.\n   - Both are in `crates/trust-but-verify/src/agent/configured.rs`.\n   - `bedrock_configuration_attaches_to_a_cache_without_being_persisted` shows the cache holds the agent, and a cloned domain shares it (`Arc::ptr_eq`).\n   - `agent_executions_isolate_conversations_and_dependency_traces` and `inputs_count_each_opening_insertion_and_each_repeated_node_read` in `crates/trust-but-verify/src/agent/tests.rs` exercise `ValidationContext::with_agent`.\n\n2. **The SDK does not persist the configuration.**\n   - The Bedrock test serializes the stored evidence. It asserts there is no `backend` key and no profile or model strings.\n   - The OpenAI test asserts the saved evidence contains none of the key, the model, `backend` or `api_key`. It checks this after each of two calls.\n\n3. **A cache created without an agent supports deterministic criteria.**\n   - `deterministic_validation_uses_required_storage_without_an_agent` in `crates/trust-but-verify/src/agent/tests.rs` uses a context with no agent. It asserts `ask` returns `NoAgentConfigured`. A deterministic `Review` criterion still verifies, stores evidence, and records a node dependency with the right fingerprint.\n   - `runner_does_not_store_a_missing_agent_error_and_supports_intermediate_calls` in `crates/trust-but-verify/src/graph/validation_tests.rs` shows a missing agent yields `NoAgentConfigured` and stores no record.\n   - `configured_agents_initialize_only_when_asked_and_report_setup_errors` shows a cache with an agent runs a deterministic question without touching the backend.\n\nThe cited `requirements.sdk.validation-cache.with_agent` obligations are covered by the same tests: lazy setup, setup errors only on an awaited ask, an empty cache, and sharing with clones. The `supported_backend_settings_create_transports_without_sending_requests` test checks transport creation without sending a request.\n\nNo behavioral obligation is left without a test that exercises it and asserts its outcome."
      }
